;; Generic mapping for an export that carries one signed amount column, as most
;; non-Japanese banks and card issuers do. Copy it, set the account, currency,
;; scale and the four column labels from the export's own header row.
;;
;; `:scale` is minor units per major unit: 1 for JPY, 100 for USD/EUR/GBP,
;; 1000 for KWD/BHD. Getting it wrong is caught for a value that carries more
;; precision than the scale allows (`:fraction-exceeds-scale`) but not for a
;; whole-unit value, so set it deliberately.
;;
;; `:ref` is optional and worth wiring when the export has one: an
;; institution-provided transaction reference is authoritative identity and
;; makes de-duplication exact instead of tuple-based.

{:mapping/institution :example-bank
 :mapping/document    :statement
 :mapping/unverified  true
 :mapping/account     :acct/example-checking
 :mapping/currency    "USD"
 :mapping/scale       100
 :mapping/date-order  :mdy      ; :ymd | :dmy | :mdy — must match the export

 :mapping/columns
 {:date        "Date"
  :description "Description"
  :amount      "Amount"        ; signed: negative is an outflow
  :ref         "Reference"}}
